much of the time when the Zimmermann  telegram is discussed the focus is often  on the German American and British  reactions to it seldom does Mexico's  part in the whole incident get a mention  of what it intended to do which  obviously raises the question how did  Mexico react to the Zimmermann telegram  so just to let everyone know the  Zimmermann telegram was a diplomatic  cable sent to Mexico from Germany in  1917 as World War one was ravaging the  continent this message named after  Arthur Zimmermann the German foreign  minister gave German financial and  political support to Mexico should it  invade the United States it promised to  recognize Mexican ownership of Texas New  Mexico and Arizona but not California or  the rest of the territory the Mexico had  lost to the US in 1848 Mexico at this  point was to put it mildly not the most  stable state in the world and had been  fighting a bloody civil war for roughly  seven years and relations with the  United States were absolutely awful  as such the Mexican government under  President Burness Tianna Carranza turned  to Germany for whatever support again  given the us-mexican tensions the  Germans felt that sending the telegram  was worth a shot one problem the  diplomatic cable had to travel through  London before it could even cross the  Atlantic it was quickly intercepted and  decoded by the British who promptly told  everyone but the Germans could have  simply denied it right yes yet they  didn't and Zimmermann publicly declared  it to be real an American opinion  rapidly shifted from isolationism to  let's go squash the Germans yet before  it was publicly known Mexico had  received the telegram so what did they  think well Carranza didn't dismiss it  straight away and given his dislike for  the United States he asked his generals  how to wage war against it the generals  came to one conclusion  fighting a war with the US would be easy  winning it would be impossible the  reasons for their conclusions were thus  one the German offers of military aid  were basically meaningless Germany could  send some u-boats but their value would  be limited which meant that all they  could really do was send some advisors  to Germany was being blockaded by the  Royal Navy and so good luck getting any  of that promised cash three Mexico was  still fighting a civil war and war was a  multiple fronts seldom and well there  was no sense fight in the u.s. when  behind the front lines revolutionaries  would be trying to overthrow the  government for Mexico's economy couldn't  handle a major war the Civil War had  done little to affect Mexico's booming  oil industry but a blockade by the u.s.  Navy would have destroyed it completely  five even if all these problems could  have been avoided the United States  would have crushed Mexico anyway  you see before this the US had briefly  occupied Veracruz in 1914 after a  diplomatic incident and there was little  doubt that they could do it again but  for the whole country as such no action  was taken by Mexico because whilst  Carranza disliked the US he wasn't  suicidal nothing was settled on about  the Zimmermann telegram because for  Mexico there was nothing to be done  it couldn't have won the war and  ultimately its leaders could see that  Germany wanted Mexico to be little more  than a speed bump to slow down American  deployment to Europe I hope you enjoyed  this episode and thank you for watching  with extra thanks to my patreon  supporters which you can see on screen  and with an extra special thanks to  James Bissonnette David archaeologist  Ozark a flash Party Boyko Rob Waterhouse  Chris wicker Michael Reynolds Gustav  Swann David Silverman spinning three  plates  Maggie packs Kowski Christian check'  Anthony Beckett Ike Skye Chappell and  Winston Cawood  you
 

